harness, and relay schemes. Deferred iOS target definitions are not generated or
built in macOS-only mode. A future resumed iOS credential-free simulator check
must use the same trust boundary but is not a macOS required check.

### 3.3 Release intake and immutable candidate preparation

`release-intake.yml` triggers on a `v*` tag push. It is unprivileged and may be
loaded from the tagged commit, so it is never a policy authority. Its sole job,
`release/request-intake`, uses `contents: read`, no environment, secrets,
cache, artifact upload, checkout, executable candidate code, publication
permission, or production network. The run record itself is diagnostic evidence
retained for 14 days. Success or failure merely completes an intake attempt and
cannot accept a candidate.

| Job / non-blocking intake check | Actor trust and input | Token / environment / secrets | Network | Outputs / retention | Approval |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `release/request-intake` | Untrusted tagged workflow revision and tag event identity; never policy or candidate authority | Repository-enforced `contents: read`; no environment; no repository/organization production secret | None | GitHub run/event metadata only; diagnostic/14d; no cache or uploaded artifact | None |

The intake boundary is enforced outside tagged YAML by repository Actions
settings (`GITHUB_TOKEN` read-only), absence of repository/organization
production secrets, and protected-environment deployment-branch rules that
admit only the protected default branch. A tagged workflow that changes its own
permissions, steps, name, or environment reference therefore gains no release
authority; disappearance or mutation of the expected intake produces no trusted
candidate.

`release-prepare.yml` triggers only on `workflow_run: completed` for the named
`Release request intake` workflow. GitHub binds this run and its workflow file
to the protected default branch. There is no selectable-ref
`workflow_dispatch` and no direct tag/push trigger on this trusted workflow.
The first job independently reads the triggering run and repository ref metadata
through the GitHub API, then requires one exact `v*` tag, an exact commit
reachable from the protected default branch, the expected event/repository, a
readable intake conclusion, `github.ref` equal to the default branch, and
`github.workflow_sha` equal to the protected default-branch workflow revision
whose SHA-256 policy digest is checked into the release-policy manifest. Intake
artifacts, caches, output strings, checkout, logs, code, and asserted conclusions
are never downloaded or executed. Missing, ambiguous, or inconsistent metadata
is `unknown` and stops before candidate acceptance.

Every credential-capable reusable workflow is called as
`owner/repository/.github/workflows/<file>.yml@<full-reviewed-commit-SHA>` and
that SHA plus file digest appears in the immutable candidate. Relative local
workflow calls and tag/branch refs are prohibited for release authority because
they resolve from mutable or caller-selected code.

| Job / blocking check | Actor trust and input | Token / environment / secrets | Network | Outputs / retention | Approval |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `release/candidate-identity` | Default-branch `workflow_run`; independently read run/ref metadata, exact default-branch-reachable candidate commit, tag/version, trusted workflow SHA and policy digest; no intake payload | `contents: read`, `actions: read`; no production environment; no secrets | GitHub repository/workflow metadata read only | Immutable candidate manifest, intake/run identity, tag/ref and workflow-provenance evidence; release-record/7y | None |
| `release/revalidate` | Exact candidate manifest | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | Same allowlists as credential-free CI | Fresh results for every active required check, with digests | None |
| `release/review-gate` | Exact manifest plus complete active evidence index | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | Deny | Machine verdict: promotable/non-promotable/unknown; release-record/7y | Recorded engineering/security/release approvals; human ratification remains `TASK-260717-2d308k` before publication |

The candidate manifest records source commit, clean-state assertion, source and
dependency locks, toolchain/SDK/runner images, protocol and relay manifests,
marketing/build versions, expected artifact names, the trusted caller workflow
SHA/policy digest, every reusable-workflow SHA/file digest, and every evidence
digest. It is immutable after `release/review-gate` starts.

### 3.4 `release-relay.yml` — relay staging

Trigger: reusable workflow call only from the exact full-SHA-pinned trusted
release workflow recorded by an accepted `release-prepare.yml` candidate.
Direct PR, branch, tag, relative local, mutable-ref, or arbitrary workflow calls
are rejected before protected-environment access.

| Job / blocking check | Actor trust and input | Token / environment / secrets | Network | Outputs / retention | Approval |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `release/relay-rebuild` | Exact source/toolchain/target manifest | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secret | Checksum-pinned tool/bootstrap sources only | Two isolated four-target trees and comparison; candidate/180d | None |
| `release/relay-compliance` | Exact rebuilt bytes | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secret | Allowlisted advisory source only | Manifest, checksums, SBOM, notices, scan, provenance; release-record/7y | Relay/security policy owners through accepted contracts |
| `release/relay-stage` | Exact compliance-approved digests | `contents: read`; protected `relay-staging`; narrowly scoped staging credential if a remote store is used | Only the named staging endpoint | Immutable digest-addressed staging receipt; release-record/7y | Environment approval by release owner |

Staging is not public promotion. A Linux runner is not required by this
workflow; any native Linux equivalence claim must cite separately accepted
evidence owned by `TASK-260715-pa6evr` and `TASK-260715-36gq4m`.

### 3.5 `release-macos.yml` — protected macOS release

Trigger: reusable workflow call only from the exact full-SHA-pinned trusted
release orchestrator recorded for one immutable candidate. Relative local and
mutable-ref calls are rejected before protected-environment access. Production concurrency group is
`relux-production-release` with `cancel-in-progress: false`.

| Job / blocking check | Actor trust and input | Token / environment / secrets | Network | Outputs / retention | Approval |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `release/macos-build-inspect` | Exact candidate and relay staging receipt; fresh build, never PR artifacts/caches | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | Pinned dependencies only | Unsigned archive inputs and inspection report; candidate/180d | None |
| `release/macos-sign-notarize` | Exact inspected bytes | `contents: read`; protected `macos-signing`; Developer ID identity/profile/password and named notary credential only | Apple notarization endpoints only | Signed app/DMG, public identity/team/profile metadata, notarization/stapling/Gatekeeper evidence; release-record/7y | macOS signing environment approver |
| `release/macos-sparkle-sign` | Final immutable notarized/stapled DMG digest | `contents: read`; protected `sparkle-signing`; Sparkle EdDSA private key only | Deny | Payload signature and proposed signed appcast; release-record/7y | Two-custodian ceremony policy plus environment approval |
| `release/macos-publish-assets` | Exact verified DMG and metadata | `contents: write`; protected `github-release`; publication token only | GitHub release endpoint only | Versioned immutable asset, checksum, stable manual-download alias receipt; release-record/7y | Release environment approval |
| `release/macos-publish-feed` | Published-asset receipt plus remote digest/header/privacy probes | Minimum feed-origin write scope; protected `update-feed`; feed credential only | Exact update origin only | Atomic feed-last receipt, signed feed and remote verification; release-record/7y | Release environment approval after asset verification |
| `release/finalize-evidence` | All exact receipts and digests | `contents: read`; no secret-bearing output | Required distribution endpoints read-only | Final evidence index and disposition; release-record/7y | Release owner |

Credential scopes are not shared across jobs. A compromised low-privilege
publication credential cannot sign, notarize, alter candidate identity, or erase
the retained evidence root. Temporary credentials are preferred; every secret
is masked and revoked/rotated after suspected exposure.

