   197	## CI/CD contract
   198	
   199	Pull requests run documentation/board validation plus builds and tests available
   200	without production credentials. Release workflows use GitHub Environments and
   201	least-privilege secrets; no certificate, private key, issuer credential, or
   202	provisioning secret is committed.
   203	
   204	Required pipelines:
   205	
   206	1. shared-core unit and protocol conformance tests on macOS;
   207	2. macOS host/system-extension build, entitlement inspection, nested signing,
   208	   notarization/stapling, final-DMG verification, Sparkle 2.9.4 payload/feed
   209	   signing, asset-first/feed-last publication, cache/privacy probes, checksums,
   210	   and stable manual-download asset;
   211	3. iOS host/extension archive, entitlement/provisioning inspection, and
   212	   TestFlight upload;
   213	4. reproducible relay cross-build matrix, tests, checksums, manifest generation,
   214	   and bundling into Apple targets;
   215	5. dependency license/SBOM and secret scanning;
   216	6. semantic version/tag validation and release notes.
   217	
   218	Production release jobs are serialized. Build artifacts retain exact source
   219	commit, dependency lockfiles, relay manifest, protocol version, bundle versions,
   220	and signing identity metadata.
   221	
   222	## App Review package
   223	
   224	The submission package includes:
   225	
   226	- an accurate VPN data-flow explanation and test SSH host instructions;
   227	- in-app VPN data disclosure and public privacy policy;
   228	- Network Extension entitlement purpose;
   229	- regional licensing notes or excluded storefronts;
   230	- explanation that users provide their own SSH exit host;
   231	- degraded-mode behavior and system-excluded traffic disclosure;
   232	- review account/profile or reproducible setup that does not expose private
   233	  production credentials.
