   104	## Security and release validation
   105	
   106	- host-key first-use/change cases and Keychain access boundaries;
   107	- malformed packet/SOCKS/SSH/relay fuzz targets with bounded allocations;
   108	- log/support-export redaction tests;
   109	- dependency licenses, notices, SBOM, pinned revisions, and relay hash manifest;
   110	- exact entitlements and nested code signatures in archived apps;
   111	- macOS notarization/stapling/Gatekeeper install; iOS/TestFlight install is
   112	  **deferred with iOS (ADR-024)** and is not a gate for the macOS-first goal;
   113	- privacy disclosure checked against actual behavior; the App Review notes check
   114	  is **deferred with the App Store branch (ADR-013)** and re-arms unchanged
   115	  before any submission.
   274	## 11. Residual risk and open evidence gates
   275	
   276	- SSH metadata remains visible and fingerprintable; the connection can be
   277	  blocked or correlated by timing and volume.
   278	- An SSH hostname may require a physical-path bootstrap DNS lookup. Pinning or
   279	  caching an endpoint changes availability and rotation tradeoffs and is not a
   280	  blanket privacy guarantee.
   281	- The exit host sees destination metadata, DNS/resolver traffic, and plaintext.
   282	- First-use host trust is vulnerable when the fingerprint is not verified out
   283	  of band.
   284	- The production SSH engine is unselected (`TASK-260715-1gjxer`); both candidate
   285	  adapters remain blocked, so host verification, channel, rekey, and memory
   286	  guarantees are not release claims.
   287	- DNS runtime limits remain non-authoritative and blocked
   288	  (`TASK-260721-3miqh4`); ADR-022 remains proposed.
   289	- Exact route exclusions and platform-scoped fail-closed behavior lack physical
   290	  macOS evidence.
   291	- The loopback SOCKS boundary is hardened but not process-private.
   292	- Relay protocol and UDP components are not yet composed through the SSH exec
   293	  stream or installed on a remote host.
   294	- Keychain, App Group, profile, signing identity, and entitlement bindings are
   295	  not yet implemented and accepted as a release configuration.
   296	- CI/signing/update credentials remain high-impact organizational trust roots;
   297	  application update generation and rollback evidence is absent.
   298	- No external penetration test, independent protocol audit, or shipped-product
   299	  privacy verification exists.
   300	- Apple platform-intent gate A0 and provisioning gate P0 remain release
   301	  boundaries; implementation evidence does not imply entitlement or review
   302	  acceptance. Scope (ADR-013/ADR-024): P0 gates the macOS-first goal and is
   303	  recorded from macOS evidence alone; A0 gates App Store distribution and iOS
   304	  submission and is deferred for the Developer ID-signed, notarized
   305	  direct-distribution macOS release, which does not pass through App Review.
